<title>FRANCE: Air France pilots strike for third day.</title>
<headline>Air France pilots strike for third day.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air France pilots stayed on strike for a third straight day Thursday, forcing the national airline to cut short-haul flights by half and medium-haul flights by 30 percent, an airline spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said long-haul flights were unaffected.</p>
<p>The stoppage, scheduled to end Friday, two days before a parliamentary election, was called after talks broke down over the carrier's plans to pay new pilots less than current crews, depending on experience.</p>
